(25: (meta: (t: semantic) (n: 1) (term: string%20value) (def: %2F%2F%20The%20readable-naming%20check%20of%20docs%2Fvision.md%23readable-english-names.%20Every%0A%2F%2F%20canonical%20name%20meta-language%20defines%20is%20a%20concept%20record%20in%0A%2F%2F%20parity%2Fnaming%2Fcanonical-concepts.json%20%28stable%20identity%2C%20readable%20phrase%2C%0A%2F%2F%20role%2C%20definition%2C%20constraints%20and%20former%20names%29%2C%20and%20the%20check%20rejects%3A%0A%2F%2F%0A%2F%2F%20-%20a%20word%20that%20is%20neither%20an%20English%20word%20in%20WordNet%203.1%20nor%20a%20registered%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20technical%20term%20%28vocabulary%29%3B%0A%2F%2F%20-%20a%20registered%20abbreviation%2C%20including%20the%20ones%20WordNet%20happens%20to%20list%20with%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20an%20unrelated%20meaning%20such%20as%20%60char%60%20or%20%60ref%60%20%28abbreviation%20expansion%29%3B%0A%2F%2F%20-%20a%20concept%20whose%20head%20is%20not%20a%20noun%2C%20or%20an%20operation%20or%20relation%20that%20does%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20not%20start%20with%20a%20verb%20%28phrase%20role%29%3B%0A%2F%2F%20-%20a%20phrase%20that%20names%20two%20different%20concepts%2C%20or%20an%20identity%20that%20is%20another%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20concept%27s%20former%20name%20%28ambiguity%29%3B%0A%2F%2F%20-%20a%20repeated%20identity%2C%20two%20names%20for%20one%20definition%2C%20two%20phrases%20WordNet%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20lists%20as%20synonyms%20word%20for%20word%20%28a%20semantic%20duplicate%2C%20unless%20the%20records%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20state%20why%20the%20concepts%20differ%29%2C%20or%20a%20representation%20that%20names%20its%20concept%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20differently%20%28duplicates%29%3B%0A%2F%2F%20-%20a%20name%20found%20in%20the%20sources%20without%20a%20record%2C%20a%20record%20no%20source%20uses%2C%20a%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20former%20name%20still%20in%20use%2C%20or%20a%20former%20name%20a%20source%20still%20decodes%20that%20its%0A%2F%2F%20%20%20record%20does%20not%20list%20%28full%20inventory%20coverage%29.%0A%0Aimport%20%7B%20existsSync%2C%20read